<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25313" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαμ-περές</span></b> , Adv., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of Place, <i>through and through, right
				through,</i> c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀσπίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.429
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				20.362
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. στέρνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					791
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βέβληαι κενεῶνα δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.284
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. οὖς</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				380
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. διὰ μέσου τοῦ [σφονδύλου]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					616e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs.,
				<i>without break, continuously,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ κεφαλῆς . . δ. ἐς πόδας ἄκρους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.640
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρη ἠλίβατος . . δ. ἀμφοτέρωθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.88
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταυροὺς . . ἔλασσε δ. ἔνθα καὶ ἔνθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δ᾽</span> [the wall] <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕσπετο πᾶσα δ.</span> all <i>in a piece,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.398
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of Time,
				<i>throughout, for ever,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.245
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				402
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				17.6
			</span></i>; pleon., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤματα πάντα δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.499
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				1.409
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Eretria</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰὲν διαμπερές</span>”
				<i>for ever and aye,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.70
				</span></i>
			. (Found in tmesi 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ δ᾽ ἀμπερές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.377
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				17.309
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμπερέως</span>: poet. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι-ανα-περές
			ʽπείρὠ.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
